  this.a6O = "1. This community keeps a shared account of what its members give to and take from each other. A unit is the measure in that account; it counts as one unit of the national currency in prices.\n2. Units are not money. They are never sold, bought or exchanged for money, by anyone.\n3. A balance above zero says how much a member has given beyond what it has taken; a balance below zero, how much it has taken beyond what it has given, and owes back to the community in its own goods and services.\n4. Each member has a credit line and a ceiling, set by the community, which may change them.\n5. Members are admitted by the community and are known to it by their real names.\n6. A sale for units is a sale. Each member issues its own invoices and pays its own taxes, in money, as for any sale.\n7. A member may leave at any time by bringing its balance to zero. A member who leaves below zero settles the difference in money within 30 days.\n8. The community may close the account of a member who breaks these rules.";
